# .vet-terms.local — org-specific terms for vet.sh's internal-hostname check.
#
# This file is gitignored and lives only on your machine. vet.sh reads it at
# staging-time so the committed, PUBLIC vet.sh script never has to hardcode
# your employer's internal tool/service names — a fixed list of those names
# baked into a public script is itself a small disclosure.
#
# One grep -E pattern fragment per line. Blank lines and lines starting with
# # are ignored. Fragments are OR'd together and checked case-insensitively
# against every added line in the staged diff.
#
# Copy this file to .vet-terms.local (same directory, no ".example") and fill
# in your own org's internal hostnames, tool names, or codenames.
#
# Example fragments (replace with your own):
# mycompany
# internal-tool-name
# vpn\.mycompany\.dev
